WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.741 --> 00:00:13.584
Narrator: Once upon a time, there lived three little pigs.

2
00:00:14.324 --> 00:00:17.385
Narrator: Their names were Curly, Chunky, and Pinky.

3
00:00:17.405 --> 00:00:21.226
Narrator: One day they decided to see the world.

4
00:00:21.246 --> 00:00:23.627
Mama: Bye-bye, boys.

5
00:00:24.007 --> 00:00:24.707
Take care.

6
00:00:24.727 --> 00:00:27.248
Curly, Chunky, and Pinky: Bye, Mama!

7
00:00:31.692 --> 00:00:34.334
Pinky: Well, I'm going this direction.

8
00:00:34.354 --> 00:00:36.976
Chunky: I'm going that way.

9
00:00:36.996 --> 00:00:40.058
Curly: I think I'll head over there.

10
00:00:40.238 --> 00:00:44.121
Narrator: The three pigs went in different directions.

11
00:00:44.141 --> 00:00:47.263
Narrator: Curly met a goat selling straw.

12
00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:50.966
Curly: I'll build a house of straw.

13
00:00:50.986 --> 00:00:55.929
Narrator: So he bought some straw and built his house.

14
00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.772
Curly: There, what a cozy home!

15
00:01:01.004 --> 00:01:02.925
Narrator: Curly relaxed in his new home.

16
00:01:03.905 --> 00:01:07.707
But there was one problem Willis: Knock-knock!

17
00:01:08.208 --> 00:01:08.988
Oh, yoo-hoo!

18
00:01:09.008 --> 00:01:11.149
Curly: Who's there?

19
00:01:11.169 --> 00:01:14.271
Willis: A friend, Willis the Wolf.

20
00:01:14.711 --> 00:01:15.671
Now let me in.

21
00:01:15.711 --> 00:01:25.256
Narrator: Mama Pig taught her sons never to open the door to strangers, [n3@especially strangers with big teeth!

22
00:01:26.516 --> 00:01:27.477
Curly: No, no!

23
00:01:27.917 --> 00:01:30.958
Not by the hair on my chinny-chin-chin.

24
00:01:30.978 --> 00:01:33.279
Willis: Let me in!

25
00:01:33.739 --> 00:01:37.241
Or I'll huff and I'll puff and I'll blow your house down.

26
00:01:37.261 --> 00:01:39.081
Curly: No!

27
00:01:39.481 --> 00:01:41.862
You can't come in, you big bully!

28
00:01:41.882 --> 00:01:44.804
Willis: I'm going to huff!

29
00:01:45.384 --> 00:01:45.964
I'm going to puff!

30
00:01:45.984 --> 00:01:49.926
Willis: And I'm going to blo-o-o-o-w-w-w your house down!

31
00:01:49.946 --> 00:01:52.767
Narrator: It wasn't that hard.

32
00:01:53.527 --> 00:01:55.368
Straw houses fall easily.

33
00:01:56.268 --> 00:01:57.489
Willis: Now, little pig.

34
00:01:58.229 --> 00:01:59.649
I'm going to eat you up!

35
00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:01.230
Curly: Help!

36
00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:06.112
Narrator: Meanwhile, Chunky met a beaver selling sticks.

37
00:02:07.453 --> 00:02:09.093
Chunky: I'll build a house of sticks.

38
00:02:09.113 --> 00:02:13.875
Narrator: So he bought some sticks and built his house.

39
00:02:15.716 --> 00:02:17.837
Chunky: There, what a pleasant home!

40
00:02:17.857 --> 00:02:21.439
Narrator: Chunky looked at his new house with pride.

41
00:02:21.459 --> 00:02:28.014
Narrator: But there was one problem Curly: Chunky, h-h-help!

42
00:02:29.555 --> 00:02:29.936
Chunky: Eek!

43
00:02:30.516 --> 00:02:31.317
It's a wolf!

44
00:02:32.097 --> 00:02:33.178
Hurry inside.

45
00:02:33.478 --> 00:02:34.419
Lock the door.

46
00:02:34.439 --> 00:02:38.923
Willis: Knock-knock!

47
00:02:39.383 --> 00:02:40.144
Let me in!

48
00:02:40.164 --> 00:02:42.205
Chunky: No!

49
00:02:42.626 --> 00:02:45.428
Not by the hair on my chinny-chin-chin.

50
00:02:45.448 --> 00:02:47.990
Willis: Let me in!

51
00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:52.294
Or I'll huff and I'll puff and I'll blow your house down.

52
00:02:52.314 --> 00:02:54.836
Chunky: You can't come in!

53
00:02:56.036 --> 00:02:57.077
Willis: I'm going to huff!

54
00:02:57.757 --> 00:02:58.618
I'm going to puff!

55
00:02:59.459 --> 00:03:02.041
Willis: And I'm going to blo-o-o-o-w-w-w your house down!

56
00:03:02.061 --> 00:03:04.422
Narrator: It wasn't that hard.

57
00:03:05.143 --> 00:03:06.604
Stick houses fall easily.

58
00:03:06.664 --> 00:03:11.047
Willis: Now I'm going to eat you up!

59
00:03:12.348 --> 00:03:12.989
Curly and Chunky: Help!

60
00:03:13.009 --> 00:03:18.733
Narrator: Meanwhile, Pinky met a horse selling bricks.

61
00:03:20.154 --> 00:03:22.356
Pinky: I'll build my house with bricks.

62
00:03:24.368 --> 00:03:27.190
Narrator: So he bought some bricks and started his house.

63
00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:30.111
Pinky: This will be a strong home.

64
00:03:30.131 --> 00:03:33.914
Narrator: Pinky took his time to build a brick house.

65
00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:37.496
Pinky: My house is almost finished.

66
00:03:38.496 --> 00:03:40.938
I'll put one more brick on the chimney.

67
00:03:40.958 --> 00:03:47.522
Narrator: But there was one problem Curly and Chunky: Pinky, h-h-help!

68
00:03:47.542 --> 00:03:51.104
Chunky: A wolf is chasing us!

69
00:03:52.292 --> 00:03:54.994
Curly: Get inside quick and lock the door!

70
00:03:55.014 --> 00:03:58.676
Willis: Well what do we have here?

71
00:04:00.256 --> 00:04:02.077
That pig is trapped on the roof.

72
00:04:02.598 --> 00:04:04.579
Willis: There's no place for him to run.

73
00:04:05.299 --> 00:04:06.820
Hello, little pig!

74
00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.822
Pinky: It's that bully, the wolf.

75
00:04:10.462 --> 00:04:11.543
What will I do?

76
00:04:11.563 --> 00:04:12.503
I know!

77
00:04:12.583 --> 00:04:16.625
Narrator: Pinky climbed into his chimney and slid down.

78
00:04:16.645 --> 00:04:21.188
Narrator: In the house, Curly and Chunky were scared.

79
00:04:22.048 --> 00:04:24.209
Curly: The wolf is chasing us!

80
00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:26.731
Chunky: He's going to eat us up!

81
00:04:26.811 --> 00:04:29.412
Pinky: I have an idea!

82
00:04:30.093 --> 00:04:31.613
Fill that pot with water.

83
00:04:31.653 --> 00:04:34.595
Narrator: Pinky built a hot fire.

84
00:04:34.615 --> 00:04:38.757
Narrator: Then the three little pigs put the pot on the fire.

85
00:04:38.777 --> 00:04:40.999
Willis: Knock-knock!

86
00:04:41.379 --> 00:04:41.819
Let me in!

87
00:04:41.839 --> 00:04:44.180
Pinky: No!

88
00:04:44.581 --> 00:04:47.402
Not by the hair on my chinny-chin-chin!

89
00:04:47.422 --> 00:04:50.124
Willis: I blew down a straw house.

90
00:04:50.904 --> 00:04:52.385
I blew down a stick house.

91
00:04:53.306 --> 00:04:57.328
Willis: I'll huff and I'll puff and I'll blow your house down too!

92
00:04:57.348 --> 00:04:59.829
Pinky: Go ahead and try!

93
00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:02.051
Willis: I'm going to huff!

94
00:05:02.891 --> 00:05:03.812
I'm going to puff!

95
00:05:04.552 --> 00:05:07.374
Willis: And I'm going to blo-o-o-o-w-w-w your house down!

96
00:05:07.394 --> 00:05:11.336
Pinky: I'm waiting!

97
00:05:11.356 --> 00:05:16.860
Willis: I said, I'm going to blo-o-o-o-w-w-w your house down!

98
00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.502
Narrator: Brick houses don't fall so easily.

99
00:05:20.582 --> 00:05:22.263
Willis: It doesn't matter.

100
00:05:23.063 --> 00:05:24.664
I can be as clever as the pig!

101
00:05:24.684 --> 00:05:28.347
Curly: Oh no, he's climbing up the house.

102
00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:30.949
Chunky: He's climbing onto the roof!

103
00:05:30.969 --> 00:05:33.230
Pinky: Let's see.

104
00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:35.852
The water is boiling nice and hot.

105
00:05:35.952 --> 00:05:40.515
Willis: I'll slide down the chimney just like that pig!

106
00:05:40.535 --> 00:05:44.598
Narrator: Willis licked his lips and hopped down the chimney.

107
00:05:44.618 --> 00:05:52.139
Narrator: But there was just one problem Narrator: When Willis fell in, Pinky covered the pot.

108
00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:54.140
Willis: Ahh!

109
00:05:54.401 --> 00:05:55.301
Oww! Let me out!

110
00:05:55.321 --> 00:05:59.705
Pinky: I'll let you out if you promise to leave us alone.

111
00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:01.726
Willis: I promise!

112
00:06:01.746 --> 00:06:05.690
Narrator: Willis left town and never came back.

113
00:06:07.071 --> 00:06:08.612
Pinky: We won't see him again!

114
00:06:08.632 --> 00:06:12.595
Curly: Well, it's time to build another house.

115
00:06:12.615 --> 00:06:14.917
Chunky: Let's get started!

116
00:06:14.937 --> 00:06:17.419
Narrator: Pinky helped his brothers.

117
00:06:18.476 --> 00:06:22.558
Narrator: When Mama Pig came, they all had new, strong brick homes.

118
00:06:23.578 --> 00:06:25.679
Mama: What beautiful homes, boys!

119
00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:29.841
I'm glad you built your houses of brick.

120
00:06:30.001 --> 00:06:32.162
Mama: You never know what might happen!

121
00:06:32.182 --> 00:06:35.263
Narrator: And the three little pigs smiled.

122
00:06:35.924 --> 00:06:36.244
The end.
